<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="eyebrow">Four ways, pick one</div>
		<h1>Install</h1>
		<p class="lede">postmarketOS is Alpine, so this is <b>apk</b>, not apt.</p>
		<div class="grid">
			<a href="install-image.html">
				<div class="n">1 &middot; Ready image</div>
				<p><b>Start here.</b> One download, everything inside, two fastboot
				commands. Wipes the phone. Not encrypted.</p></a>
			<a href="install-repo.html">
				<div class="n">2 &middot; On a phone already running pmOS</div>
				<p>Three commands. Keeps your data. Brings the kernel, so the reboot is
				a separate step.</p></a>
			<a href="install-pmos.html">
				<div class="n">3 &middot; Install postmarketOS yourself first</div>
				<p>U-Boot for your panel, pmbootstrap, then route 2. For a phone that
				has never run Linux.</p></a>
			<a href="install-encrypted.html">
				<div class="n">4 &middot; Encrypted</div>
				<p>Build it yourself, one command. There is no encrypted image to
				download, and that is deliberate.</p></a>
		</div>
		<div class="note"><i></i><div>
			<b>One rule on this phone, whatever route you take.</b>
			<code>boot</code> holds U-Boot, not the kernel. Flash the system to
			<code>userdata</code>. <code>fastboot flash boot &lt;kernel&gt;</code> leaves
			the phone unable to boot at all.
		</div></div>
	</div>
</section>
